   - Car 2 (the second car) is traveling at **70 miles per hour**.

2. **Determine the relative speed:**
   - Since both cars are moving in the same direction (on a highway), the **relative speed** (the rate at which the distance between the two cars changes) is the difference between their speeds:
     $$
     \text{Relative speed} = 70 - 60 = 10 \text{ miles per hour}
     $$

